{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1006911-watchtowers-an-elevator-pitch","id":1006911,"title":"Watchtowers an elevator pitch?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T17:11:28-08:00","id":1006911,"title":"Watchtowers an elevator pitch?","content":"So I'll be picking up my Boston mage game after a several year hiatus from mage. I was wanting to run my players through a pre awakening game and play out them learning about watchtowers and choosing a path. Without dropping a book down in front of them I'd like to give a good short summary of each path. Does anyone have some suggestions or short write ups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:01:19-08:00","id":1006931,"title":"","content":"It's not like the write-ups on Paths in the book are very long.<br /> <br /> Instead of making your players choose though the other way to go is to listen to their character concept and then suggest what you think fits best. That worked with my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:02:54-08:00","id":1006934,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the corebook quick character creation page includes a sentence depicting each splat, and arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:34:32-08:00","id":1007001,"title":"","content":"It does not, but as has already been suggested, it usually won't be hard to figure out who belongs on what Path. Just make a suggestion based on character concept and chat it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:01:18-08:00","id":1007297,"title":"","content":"Or let them choose two Arcana, with one more important. That important will indicate Path of character - if character will not work with Path archetype in some way ( I'm still to behold character like this after maybe 30 PCs created like that ), advise reversing Arcanum priority. And there you are done - and players are happy as they get Arcana they wanted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I 'discovered' that Ruling Arcana of Paths are most organic to Paths concepts, so they easily go hand in hand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-23-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:28:19-08:00","id":1007376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1006911-watchtowers-an-elevator-pitch?p=1007001#post1007001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not, but as has already been suggested, it usually won't be hard to figure out who belongs on what Path. Just make a suggestion based on character concept and chat it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, crap.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Stn43UM.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Jo82dmF.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/epTskbA.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Gotta add the second archetype for 2e in the Paths, the Seers of the Throne, some changes to Arcana from 2e and maybe Apostates/Nameless Orders, but that should cut it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:56:54-08:00","id":1007386,"title":"","content":"Uh... Pages 19 and 35 of second edition? That have the short blurbs for the Paths and Orders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:09:35-08:00","id":1007392,"title":"","content":"To answer the prompt, I've sort of loosely categorized the awakenings in terms of their metaphorical origin with respect to the fallen world:<br /> <br /> Obrimoi awaken from <b>above</b>. Their Watchtower floats in the sky surrounded by angelic beings. They literally command divine powers of Forces and Prime. Obrimos awakenings deal with trying to <b>descend</b> from the Aether.<br /> <br /> Moroi awaken from <b>below</b>. Their Watchtower sinks heavy in the river, surrounded by the lost and the dead. They have control over the earthy domains of Death and Matter. Moros awakenings deal with trying to <b>rise up </b>above the Stygia.<br /> <br /> Mastigoi awaken from <b>inside</b>. Their Watchtower sits fixed in fire and iron and is surrounded by daemonic creatures. They have dominion over the expanses of Mind and Space. Mastigos awakenings deal with trying to <b>break out</b> of the prison of Pandemonium.<br /> <br /> Thrysoi awaken from <b>outside</b>. Their Watchtower grows out of the flora and fauna and is surrounded by living creatures and otherworldly spirits. They reign over the Life and Spirit. Thyrus awakenings deal with trying to <b>come back </b>from the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> Acanthia awaken from <b>without</b>. Their Watchtower cares not for time or reason, existing in a mercurial state outside of causality, surrounded by faeries and dream creatures. They are masters of, or mastered by, Time and Fate. Acanthus awakenings deal with trying to <b>reconcile </b>Arcadia with the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Of course there are the descriptions in the book, but these are what I offered new players as the conceptual differences between the different Path awakenings.<br /> <br /> EDITED to fix my Greek plurals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 11-23-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:42:03-08:00","id":1007408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1006911-watchtowers-an-elevator-pitch?p=1007392#post1007392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer the prompt, I've sort of loosely categorized the awakenings in terms of their metaphorical origin with respect to the fallen world:<br /> <br /> Obrimoi awaken from <b>above</b>. Their Watchtower floats in the sky surrounded by angelic beings. They literally command divine powers of Forces and Prime. Obrimos awakenings deal with trying to <b>descend</b> from the Aether.<br /> <br /> Moroi awaken from <b>below</b>. Their Watchtower sinks heavy in the river, surrounded by the lost and the dead. They have control over the earthy domains of Death and Matter. Moros awakenings deal with trying to <b>rise up </b>above the Stygia.<br /> <br /> Mastigoi awaken from <b>inside</b>. Their Watchtower sits fixed in fire and iron and is surrounded by daemonic creatures. They have dominion over the expanses of Mind and Space. Mastigos awakenings deal with trying to <b>break out</b> of the prison of Pandemonium.<br /> <br /> Thrysoi awaken from <b>outside</b>. Their Watchtower grows out of the flora and fauna and is surrounded by living creatures and otherworldly spirits. They reign over the Life and Spirit. Thyrus awakenings deal with trying to <b>come back </b>from the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> Acanthia awaken from <b>without</b>. Their Watchtower cares not for time or reason, existing in a mercurial state outside of causality, surrounded by faeries and dream creatures. They are masters of, or mastered by, Time and Fate. Acanthus awakenings deal with trying to <b>reconcile </b>Arcadia with the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Of course there are the descriptions in the book, but these are what I offered new players as the conceptual differences between the different Path awakenings.<br /> <br /> EDITED to fix my Greek plurals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool this is more along the lines of suggestions I was looking for. There are some short descriptions in the book but those didn't really grab me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:51:25-08:00","id":1012554,"title":"","content":"Here what i use for my own pitches<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimo\u00ef </b>awaken in the fire of revelation, they command the Forces of the universe and command the Prime essence of truth and magic.They are mighty lords and summoners of angels, clad in lightning and wielder of sacred flame<br /> <br /> <b>Moro\u00ef </b>awaken in the quiet of the grave, they command Death the realm of shadows and ghosts and the Matter of the universe. They are lords of the dead, the inanimate, alchemists and necromancers surrounded by the shades of the departed.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigo\u00ef</b> awaken to the screaming of their own minds. They command Mind and Space, arcanas of the connection and they realize separation is the greatest lie ever told. They are lord of the immaterial, twisting desires and sympathies to their whim. Some summon their own shackled sins to their aid.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsii </b>awaken to the grandeur of life, its brillance, its magnificence. They command all Life and the Spirits, reflections of the world, bow to them. They are lords over the inhuman, commanding both animals and bestial spirits. They are health, life and strenght all manifest.<br /> <br /> <b>Acanthii </b>awaken to the splitting of destinies. They see through Time and all Fate are theirs to weave. They are subtle lords over causality itself. With a gesture time reverses its course, with a gesture they decreed dooms on their ennemies. Brothers to the Fae they wander in search of consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: Sorry for the necromancy, didn't saw the date. Still it could be interesting to see how other STs presents the Watchtowers</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T21:25:47-08:00","id":1012979,"title":"","content":"I just realized the best elevator pitches for the different watchtowers are probably in the Gnosis section on page 85. The descriptions on how each path sees the world are really insightful and exactly what I'd want my players to know if they were picking a path for their characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T22:13:04-08:00","id":1013005,"title":"","content":"When matching a Watchtower to a character I usually do it by personality types, especially if the character's personality was supposed to have been changed by the experience.<br /> \u200bObrimos: These people are driven by a higher purpose, serving something greater than themselves. They are driven, goal oriented and not given to self doubt or existential crisis.<br /> <br /> Arcanthus: Everything is luck and happenstance, only these people know that luck is a skill and happenstance is what happens when all of the little things add up to something big. To the Arcanthus everything happens for a reason, witting or not someone made it happen.<br /> <br /> Moros: He lives in a world of hammers, big hammers or small, with the right hammer you can do anything. Even the supposedly ephemeral ghost can be taken in hand and hammered into shape.<br /> <br /> \u200bMastigos: This character is all to aware of his flaws, something he knows everyone has. This makes him humble and tolerant, he doesn't judge his worth or that of others by their flaws. He also tends to see those flaws as challenges that can make people stronger, but there will always be another flaw.<br /> <br /> \u200bThyrsus: This guy lives in the moment, taking everything for what it is, not what he thinks it can be. He acts, thinking and planning have their place but not if all you do is think about doing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 12-06-2016, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T01:35:43-08:00","id":1013066,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey. I have a bunch of this kind of thing, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979372-what-does-it-mean-to-walk-a-path-interpretations#post979372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acanthus<br /> The Acanthus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>agency</b>. Everyone lives a scripted life, walking through the motions as actors on a stage. That\u2019s the story that the world tells, and you\u2019re just a face in that crowd, looking busy, lacking meaning. The Acanthus take control of the narrative, and thereby power over their life and the consequent world around them. They diverge from the script and say, \u201cYes, I can. And I will <i>because </i>I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mastigos<br /> The Mastigos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>relationships</b>. Everyone lies to each other, putting up outward facades while their inner life is in turmoil. They turn away from each other and themselves, refusing to acknowledge necessary truths, poisoning their community. The Mastigos say that, \u201cDistance is a Lie.\u201d They forcibly create bridges where there were walls, and relish in the growing pains that come with having to come face-to-face with both others and oneself.<br /> <br /> Moros<br /> The Moros is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>components</b>. Everyone has a fixed notion of what constitutes an object, that lead is lead and gold is gold, that a child is a child and a man is a man. They go through their lives trying to acquire new things, ignoring that they could patch together everything they need from what they already have. The Moros breaks free of this attitude, reducing complexities into simple construction blocks and rebuilding them into something greater than the original arrangements. They watch and guide the transition from youth to age, from desolation to creation, from past to future.<br /> <br /> Obrimos<br /> The Obrimos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>keystones</b>. Everyone presumes that things are disparate and disconnected, that you can manipulate one thing without affecting anything else. That\u2019s what it looks like on the outside: the superficial facade that people see everyday. The Obrimos understands that beneath such illusions is the hard truth of energy cycling through systems underlying the reality. They find the key that binds a thousand worlds together and turn it, opening a thousand locks at once and freeing a thousand minds with a single word, \u201cSee.\u201d<br /> <br /> Thyrsus<br /> The Thyrsus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>negotiations</b>. Everyone sees an inanimate world, a terra nullius uncultivated and ripe for the taking. They can\u2019t see that something was already there, something that deserves consideration and comprehension. The Thyrsus hears these indigenous voices, speaks on their behalf, and answers them in return. The worlds are full of their own peoples, and those peoples must be accounted for when you endeavor their lands in your own right. It doesn\u2019t matter that a world might be within a person, or beyond a veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:27:53-08:00","id":1013120,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Apparently I don't know how to upload images or delete mistaken posts. Please ignore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:36:49-08:00","id":1013784,"title":"","content":"These are definitely inspirational. Pretty cool stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"